Further to my earlier letter, on thinking it over I think the answer  
is dependent on the relative probabilities of the two  
interpretations.  For example, I wouldn't have any doubt about  
"pretty (girl's school) over (pretty girl's) school.  With (large  
men's clothing) store vs large (men's clothing store) I might have  
some doubt, since both exist.  I would probably interpret (German  
book) store instead of German (book store) but Ottawa (book store)  
rather than (Ottawa book) store.


